 us-east rolled to v2.3.0 and the rollout halted with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1). A retry completed the rollout to v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west. (3) Post-rollback status: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure cause, and check the orchestrator partial-failure behavior before the next rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was only in staging and is also unhealthy. No change-manager approval was needed, since v2.3.0 has been healthy in production.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across versions. I retried the same rollback once, and it completed in all regions.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure and retry, and the post-rollback status. It also lists two follow-ups: find the cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator's partial-failure behavior before the next rollout.", "type": "text"}]}]}